<p>Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi met Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi in Beijing on Wednesday, his first visit to China since the U.S.-Israeli war on Iran began, Chinese state media and Iranian reports said. Iran’s Foreign Ministry said Araghchi would discuss bilateral relations and regional and international developments. Xinhua initially gave no further details on the talks. The meeting took place ahead of President Trump’s scheduled May 14-15 visit to Beijing for talks with Chinese President Xi Jinping. U.S. officials have urged Beijing to use its relationship with Tehran to press Iran over the Strait of Hormuz, a key energy shipping route, with Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent saying Trump and Xi would discuss Iran during their summit. President Trump paused a U.S. escort operation through the strait as Washington sought an agreement with Iran.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/dJUCT-PSCLiREdH06xP7-XBJNm3GhMOxlPn1EKshcIBaPEgXLiZO7Q2ho-PSF7iOxZUsYkHqI-j958I_YyUApLNvDkq3zGyQEgCuAPsqcKXfXTuFv50WhvxA8EfxmMsZE0C1PNdkh-qbz8sJnIix_mpfSP_r9-BZGwwtH3Avm7qSBUX_C5WTgB3FeL55a-7ZjRH8-KqTrtCkij68fZcu4y722oMwu5C8DcL8bi2XeqSplOM4J1sVumylM22feOTrkatknA' alt='Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi and Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi shake hands in Beijing on May 6.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Oil link: China is described as a key customer for Iranian oil despite U.S. sanctions aimed at limiting Tehran’s revenue.</li><li>Prior contacts: Wang and Araghchi held several phone calls after U.S.-Israeli strikes on Iran began in late February and before Wednesday’s in-person meeting.</li><li>UN pressure: Bessent urged China and Russia to stop blocking United Nations initiatives, including a resolution encouraging steps to protect commercial shipping in the Strait of Hormuz.</li><li>Visit format: Araghchi’s trip was described as a one-day visit, with Iranian media reporting that he arrived in Beijing on Wednesday morning.</li></ul><blockquote>Join us in this international operation - Scott Bessent</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United States: Secretary of State Marco Rubio urged Beijing to deliver a firm message to Araghchi and press Iran to reduce restrictions in the Strait of Hormuz, warning that Iran risked global isolation. (<a href='https://www.digi24.ro/stiri/externe/ministrul-iranian-de-externe-a-ajuns-la-beijing-marco-rubio-chinezii-sa-ii-spuna-lui-araghchi-ce-trebuie-sa-auda-3758217'>Digi24</a>, <a href='https://news.nextapple.com/international/20260506/8E25F143F8E64280B0B3D489A0105A70'>Next Apple</a>)</li><li>China: Wang Yi called the U.S.-Israeli war on Iran “illegitimate” and urged a complete ceasefire, according to Iranian state media. (<a href='https://presstv.ir/Detail/2026/05/06/768119/Iranian-FM-meets-with-Chinese-counterpart-in-Beijing,-holds-diplomatic-consultations-'>Press TV</a>)</li><li>Financial Times analysts: Analysts cited by the Financial Times said Xi could use China’s relationship with Tehran as leverage in talks with President Trump. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/f932425a-5023-426e-ae89-1521dbbfc07a'>Financial Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/06/world/asia/china-iran-us-trump-hormuz.html'>China Meets Iranian Official as U.S. Demands Strait of Hormuz Open</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/f932425a-5023-426e-ae89-1521dbbfc07a'>Iran’s top diplomat visits China ahead of Trump-Xi summit</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iranian-foreign-minister-araghchi-chinese-counterpart-wang-yi-meeting-in-beijing-amid-west-asia-crisis/article70945539.ece'>Iranian Foreign Minister Araghchi meets Chinese counterpart Wang Yi in Beijing</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/05/irans-araghchi-heads-china-us-presses-beijing-over-hormuz-what-know'>Iran’s Araghchi heads to China as US presses Beijing over Hormuz: What to know</a> - al-monitor.co